-- ----- fragment: minion_isaiah_30.sql (Isaiah 30) -----
-- Chapter: Isaiah 30 — WOE to the rebellious children who go down to Egypt for help (trust in the
-- arm of flesh). *Woe to the rebellious children... that walk to go down into Egypt... to trust in
-- the shadow of Egypt* (30:1-2); the cure is teshuvah, not cavalry: *In returning and rest shall ye
-- be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength: and ye would not* (30:15) — and
-- *But ye said, No; for we will flee upon horses* (30:16). The Teacher's voice is restored to a
-- chastened people: *thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in
-- it* (30:21), and *thine eyes shall see thy teachers* (30:20). The idols are defiled and cast off:
-- *thou shalt cast them away as a menstruous cloth* (30:22). And the day of judgment comes: *the
-- name of Yahuah (LORD) cometh from far, burning with his anger* (30:27); *Tophet is ordained of
-- old* (30:33).
-- Tag: isa30   Temp view: _s303_isa30_lookup
-- Sort band: base 26725, step 3 -> threads at 26725, 26728, 26731, 26734 (4 threads)
-- Source of EVERY row: 'canon','isaiah',30,v
--
-- Isaiah 30 coverage:
--   ★★ v.1-2 + v.15-16 (Woe to the rebellious children... to trust in the shadow of Egypt; In
--          returning and rest shall ye be saved... and ye would not; But ye said, No; for we will
--          flee upon horses)
--        NT:     ★★ Matthew 11:28-29 (Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I
--                will give you rest... and ye shall find rest unto your souls) — THREAD 1 (the rest
--                of 30:15 fulfilled in the Formed Son; returning-and-rest, the yoke that gives rest)
--        Extras: none warranted (the trust-in-flesh rebuke is fully carried in canon)
--        Tanakh: ★★ Isaiah 31:1 (Woe to them that go down to Egypt for help; and stay on horses...
--                but they look not unto the Holy One of Yashar'el), ★ Hosea 14:3 (Asshur shall not
--                save us; we will not ride upon horses) + Hosea 14:1 (O Yashar'el, return unto Yahuah
--                Elohayka), ★ Deuteronomy 17:16 (he shall not multiply horses... nor cause the people
--                to return to Egypt) — THREAD 1 (the trust-in-Egypt/horses rebuke; the teshuvah call)
--   ★ v.20-21 (thine eyes shall see thy teachers; thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying,
--          This is the way, walk ye in it)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the Teacher's voice is the canon's own restored-instruction
--                figure; the Good-Shepherd voice woven in prose, not forced to one verse)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Psalm 32:8 (I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I
--                will guide thee with mine eye) + Psalm 32:9 (the bit and bridle) — THREAD 2 (the
--                Teacher's voice behind thee; this is the way, walk ye in it)
--   ★ v.22 (Ye shall defile also the covering of thy graven images of silver... thou shalt cast them
--          away as a menstruous cloth)
--        NT:     none warranted (the idol-casting is the Tanakh's own restoration motif)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Isaiah 31:7 (in that day every man shall cast away his idols of silver, and his
--                idols of gold), ★ Hosea 14:8 (Ephraim shall say, What have I to do any more with
--                idols?), Isaiah 2:20 (a man shall cast his idols of silver... to the moles) — THREAD 3
--   ★ v.27 + v.33 (the name of Yahuah cometh from far, burning with his anger... Tophet is ordained
--          of old; yea, for the king it is prepared)
--        NT:     none warranted distinct (the day-of-Yahuah fire is held in the canon's lawsuit frame)
--        Extras: none warranted
--        Tanakh: ★ Jeremiah 7:31 (they have built the high places of Tophet... to burn their sons),
--                Jeremiah 7:32 (it shall no more be called Tophet... but the valley of slaughter) —
--                THREAD 4 (the Name from far; Tophet ordained, the judgment-fire)
--   v.3-14 (Zoan/Hanes; the rebellious lying children that will not hear the law of Yahuah; the breach
--          ready to fall) — woven into THREAD 1's prose (the Egypt-trust verdict); v.9 *children that
--          will not hear the law of Yahuah* is the Torah-rejection at the root of the woe (named in
--          THREAD 1). No separate add.
--   v.17-19 (the beacon on the mountain; Yahuah waits to be gracious; the people dwell in Zion) —
--          the grace-after-judgment turn, preface to the teachers of THREAD 2; woven in prose.
--   v.23-26 (the rain of thy seed; the light of the moon as the sun; the day Yahuah bindeth up the
--          breach) — the restoration-blessing after teshuvah; woven into THREAD 2/THREAD 4 prose
--          (the healing of *the stroke of their wound*, 30:26). No separate add forced.
--   v.28-32 (the breath as an overflowing stream; the song as in the night when a holy solemnity is
--          kept; the Assyrian beaten down) — the judgment-and-song; *a holy solemnity* (30:29) is the
--          appointed-feast note, woven into THREAD 4 prose. No separate add.
--
-- Threads (slug — target libraries):
--   1. isaiah-30-in-returning-and-rest-shall-ye-be-saved — NT (Matthew 11) + Tanakh (Isaiah 31,
--      Hosea 14, Deuteronomy 17) [free]
--      (★★ the teshuvah keystone; trust not in Egypt/horses but in Yahuah; the rest the Son gives)
--   2. isaiah-30-this-is-the-way-walk-ye-in-it — Tanakh (Psalm 32) [free]
--      (★ the Teacher's voice behind thee; the restored teachers; instructed in the way to go)
--   3. isaiah-30-cast-them-away-as-a-menstruous-cloth — Tanakh (Isaiah 31, Hosea 14, Isaiah 2) [free]
--      (★ the idols of silver and gold defiled and cast off in the day of return)
--   4. isaiah-30-the-name-of-yahuah-cometh-from-far-tophet-ordained — Tanakh (Jeremiah 7) [free]
--      (★ the Name from far burning with anger; Tophet ordained, the judgment-fire)
--
-- Framing notes:
--   ★★ RETURNING AND REST (THREAD 1): The chapter opens with the woe — *Woe to the rebellious
--      children, saith Yahuah (LORD), that take counsel, but not of me... That walk to go down into
--      Egypt... to trust in the shadow of Egypt* (30:1-2) — and names the cure as covenant-faithful
--      trust, not cavalry: *In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence
--      shall be your strength: and ye would not* (30:15). The refusal is *But ye said, No; for we will
--      flee upon horses* (30:16). Isaiah's next chapter says it again: *Woe to them that go down to
--      Egypt for help; and stay on horses... but they look not unto the Holy One of Yashar'el
--      (Israel)* (31:1). Hosea makes it the very confession of return: *Asshur shall not save us; we
--      will not ride upon horses* (14:3), *O Yashar'el (Israel), return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD
--      thy God)* (14:1). And the Torah forbade the Egypt-and-horses reflex from the start: *he shall
--      not multiply horses to himself, nor cause the people to return to Egypt* (Deuteronomy 17:16).
--      The rest of 30:15 is the rest the Formed Son gives: *Come unto me, all ye that labour and are
--      heavy laden, and I will give you rest... and ye shall find rest unto your souls* (Matthew
--      11:28-29) — returning to him IS the returning-and-rest. Covenant-faithfulness, not the arm of
--      flesh; trust, not Egypt.
--   ★ THIS IS THE WAY (THREAD 2): To a chastened people the Teacher is restored — *though Yahuah
--      (Lord) give you the bread of adversity, and the water of affliction, yet shall not thy
--      teachers be removed into a corner any more, but thine eyes shall see thy teachers* (30:20) —
--      and his voice goes before: *thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way,
--      walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left* (30:21). That is
--      the very promise of the Psalm: *I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou
--      shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye. Be ye not as the horse, or as the mule... whose
--      mouth must be held in with bit and bridle* (Psalm 32:8-9) — the guided way against the
--      horse-and-mule that has no understanding (the same horses 30:16 fled upon). The Torah-rejecting
--      children of 30:9 (*children that will not hear the law of Yahuah*) are turned back to a people
--      whose eyes see their teachers and whose ears hear the way.
--   ★ CAST THEM AWAY (THREAD 3): The fruit of return is the idols cast off — *Ye shall defile also
--      the covering of thy graven images of silver, and the ornament of thy molten images of gold:
--      thou shalt cast them away as a menstruous cloth; thou shalt say unto it, Get thee hence*
--      (30:22). Isaiah's next chapter promises the same day: *in that day every man shall cast away
--      his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which your own hands have made unto you for a sin*
--      (31:7). Hosea gives Ephraim's repentant word: *Ephraim shall say, What have I to do any more
--      with idols?* (14:8). The day of Yahuah strips the silver and gold idols from his returning
--      people (Isaiah 2:20). Return and the idols go.
--   ★ THE NAME FROM FAR; TOPHET ORDAINED (THREAD 4): The judgment side of the day — *Behold, the
--      name of Yahuah (LORD) cometh from far, burning with his anger... his lips are full of
--      indignation, and his tongue as a devouring fire* (30:27) — and the prepared fire: *For Tophet
--      is ordained of old; yea, for the king it is prepared; he hath made it deep and large: the pile
--      thereof is fire and much wood; the breath of Yahuah (LORD), like a stream of brimstone, doth
--      kindle it* (30:33). Jeremiah names that same Tophet, the valley of the son of Hinnom, turned
--      from the place of abomination into the valley of slaughter: *they have built the high places of
--      Tophet, which is in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to burn their sons and their daughters in
--      the fire* (7:31); *it shall no more be called Tophet... but the valley of slaughter* (7:32).
--      The judgment-fire is for the oppressor (the Assyrian beaten down, 30:31), and for his people it
--      is the night of *a holy solemnity* and a song (30:29) — the healing of *the stroke of their
--      wound* (30:26). Covenant-lawsuit, not ethnic wrath; the fire is ordained against the system of
--      rebellion, and the returning remnant sings.
--   VERSES WITH NO SEPARATE ADD: v.3-8 (Zoan/Hanes, the shame of Egypt — the Egypt-trust verdict of
--      THREAD 1), v.9-14 (the lying children, the breach ready to fall — the Torah-rejection root,
--      named in THREAD 1/2 prose), v.17-19 (the beacon, Yahuah waits to be gracious — preface to
--      THREAD 2), v.23-26 (the rain of seed, moon as sun, breach bound up — restoration-blessing,
--      THREAD 2/4 prose), v.28-32 (the breath/sieve, the song, the Assyrian — THREAD 4 prose). All
--      recorded, none silently skipped.

CREATE TEMP VIEW _s303_isa30_lookup AS
SELECT e.slug AS edition_slug, b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id=c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id=b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id=e.id
 WHERE e.slug IN ('canon','enoch','jubilees','jasher','apocrypha','apocrypha-charles-vol1','pseudepigrapha','adam-eve-conflict','apocalypse-of-abraham','ascension-isaiah','sonnini-acts-29');

INSERT INTO cross_references (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source, note, tier_required)
SELECT sv.verse_id, tv.verse_id, 'manual', i.note, i.tier::content_tier
  FROM (VALUES
    -- THREAD 1 (★★): In returning and rest shall ye be saved — trust not in Egypt/horses
    ('canon','isaiah',30,15,'canon','matthew',11,28,'free',
      E'*Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest* (Matthew 11:28). The salvation of *In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength: and ye would not* (Isaiah 30:15) is the rest the Formed Son gives: returning to him IS the returning-and-rest the rebellious children refused. Not the arm of Egypt, not horses — *come unto me... and I will give you rest*.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',30,15,'canon','matthew',11,29,'free',
      E'*Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls* (Matthew 11:29). *In quietness and in confidence shall be your strength* (Isaiah 30:15) is the soul-rest of the easy yoke; the strength is in trust, not in fleeing upon horses (30:16). *Ye shall find rest unto your souls* — the very rest *ye would not* take from Yahuah is offered again in the Son.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',30,1,'canon','isaiah',31,1,'free',
      E'*Woe to them that go down to Egypt for help; and stay on horses, and trust in chariots, because they are many; and in horsemen, because they are very strong; but they look not unto the Holy One of Yashar''el (Israel), neither seek Yahuah (LORD)!* (Isaiah 31:1). The same woe as *Woe to the rebellious children... that walk to go down into Egypt... to trust in the shadow of Egypt* (Isaiah 30:1-2): the sin is trusting the arm of flesh and not looking to the Holy One of Yashar''el. Two woes, one rebuke — covenant-faithfulness against the strength of Pharaoh.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',30,16,'canon','hosea',14,3,'free',
      E'*Asshur shall not save us; we will not ride upon horses: neither will we say any more to the work of our hands, Ye are our gods* (Hosea 14:3). Hosea puts the cure in the mouth of the returning people — the exact reversal of *But ye said, No; for we will flee upon horses* (Isaiah 30:16). The horses Yashar''el fled upon are renounced in the confession of return; not Asshur, not Egypt, not horses, but Yahuah.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',30,15,'canon','hosea',14,1,'free',
      E'*O Yashar''el (Israel), return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God); for thou hast fallen by thine iniquity* (Hosea 14:1). This is the *returning* of *In returning and rest shall ye be saved* (Isaiah 30:15) — the teshuvah call to the same two-house people. The salvation Isaiah names is the return Hosea commands: *return unto Yahuah Elohayka* — and live.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',30,16,'canon','deuteronomy',17,16,'free',
      E'*But he shall not multiply horses to himself, nor cause the people to return to Egypt, to the end that he should multiply horses: forasmuch as Yahuah (LORD) hath said unto you, Ye shall henceforth return no more that way* (Deuteronomy 17:16). The Torah forbade the very reflex Isaiah rebukes — *We will flee upon horses* and the going down to Egypt (Isaiah 30:16, 30:2). The covenant said *return no more that way*; the rebellious children turned back to Egypt and to horses anyway. The woe is a Torah-breach.'),

    -- THREAD 2 (★): This is the way, walk ye in it — the Teacher's voice restored
    ('canon','isaiah',30,21,'canon','psalms',32,8,'free',
      E'*I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye* (Psalm 32:8). The promise *thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left* (Isaiah 30:21) is the very teaching-voice of the Psalm: instructed and taught *in the way which thou shalt go*, guided turn by turn. The restored Teacher whose voice goes before the chastened people.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',30,21,'canon','psalms',32,9,'free',
      E'*Be ye not as the horse, or as the mule, which have no understanding: whose mouth must be held in with bit and bridle, lest they come near unto thee* (Psalm 32:9). The word *behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it* (Isaiah 30:21) is for those who hear and understand — not the horse and mule who must be reined. It is the same horse the rebels fled upon (30:16); the guided way is the alternative to the bridled beast that has no understanding.'),

    -- THREAD 3 (★): Cast them away as a menstruous cloth — the idols of silver and gold cast off
    ('canon','isaiah',30,22,'canon','isaiah',31,7,'free',
      E'*For in that day every man shall cast away his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which your own hands have made unto you for a sin* (Isaiah 31:7). The fruit of return in *Ye shall defile also the covering of thy graven images of silver, and the ornament of thy molten images of gold: thou shalt cast them away as a menstruous cloth* (Isaiah 30:22) is named again in the next chapter: in that day the idols of silver and gold, the work of their own hands, are cast away. Return and the idols go.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',30,22,'canon','hosea',14,8,'free',
      E'*Ephraim shall say, What have I to do any more with idols? I have heard him, and observed him* (Hosea 14:8). The casting-off of *thou shalt cast them away as a menstruous cloth; thou shalt say unto it, Get thee hence* (Isaiah 30:22) is Ephraim''s own repentant word — *What have I to do any more with idols?* The northern house that filled the land with images renounces them in the day of return. Get thee hence.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',30,22,'canon','isaiah',2,20,'free',
      E'*In that day a man shall cast his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which they made each one for himself to worship, to the moles and to the bats* (Isaiah 2:20). The day of Yahuah strips the silver and gold idols from his people — the same *idols of silver* and *images of gold* of Isaiah 30:22, flung to the moles and the bats. When the Holy One is feared, the handmade gods are thrown away.'),

    -- THREAD 4 (★): The name of Yahuah cometh from far; Tophet is ordained
    ('canon','isaiah',30,33,'canon','jeremiah',7,31,'free',
      E'*And they have built the high places of Tophet, which is in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to burn their sons and their daughters in the fire; which I commanded them not, neither came it into my heart* (Jeremiah 7:31). The judgment-place of *For Tophet is ordained of old; yea, for the king it is prepared; he hath made it deep and large: the pile thereof is fire and much wood* (Isaiah 30:33) is the very Tophet of the valley of Hinnom — the place of the fire. The pit the rebels made for their abominations becomes the ordained fire of judgment.'),
    ('canon','isaiah',30,33,'canon','jeremiah',7,32,'free',
      E'*Therefore, behold, the days come, saith Yahuah (LORD), that it shall no more be called Tophet, nor the valley of the son of Hinnom, but the valley of slaughter: for they shall bury in Tophet, till there be no place* (Jeremiah 7:32). The Tophet *ordained of old... deep and large* (Isaiah 30:33) becomes the valley of slaughter — *the breath of Yahuah (LORD), like a stream of brimstone, doth kindle it* (30:33). The Name that *cometh from far, burning with his anger* (30:27) makes the place of abomination the place of judgment-fire.')
  ) AS i(src_edition,src_slug,src_ch,src_v,tgt_edition,tgt_slug,tgt_ch,tgt_v,tier,note)
  JOIN _s303_isa30_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug=i.src_edition AND sv.book_slug=i.src_slug AND sv.chapter_number=i.src_ch AND sv.verse_number=i.src_v
  JOIN _s303_isa30_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug=i.tgt_edition AND tv.book_slug=i.tgt_slug AND tv.chapter_number=i.tgt_ch AND tv.verse_number=i.tgt_v
 WHERE sv.verse_id <> tv.verse_id
ON CONFLICT (source_verse_id, target_verse_id, source) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-30-in-returning-and-rest-shall-ye-be-saved',
       E'In returning and rest shall ye be saved — trust not in Egypt, but in Yahuah',
       E'The chapter opens with a woe over the trust-in-the-arm-of-flesh reflex: *Woe to the rebellious children, saith Yahuah (LORD), that take counsel, but not of me... That walk to go down into Egypt, and have not asked at my mouth; to strengthen themselves in the strength of Pharaoh, and to trust in the shadow of Egypt!* (Isaiah 30:1-2). The cure is not cavalry but covenant-faithful trust — teshuvah: *In returning and rest shall ye be saved; in quietness and in confidence shall be your strength: and ye would not* (30:15). And the refusal is named: *But ye said, No; for we will flee upon horses; therefore shall ye flee* (30:16). Isaiah''s next chapter strikes the same note — *Woe to them that go down to Egypt for help; and stay on horses, and trust in chariots, because they are many... but they look not unto the Holy One of Yashar''el (Israel), neither seek Yahuah (LORD)!* (Isaiah 31:1). Hosea puts the reversal in the mouth of the returning people: *Asshur shall not save us; we will not ride upon horses* (14:3), and calls it home — *O Yashar''el (Israel), return unto Yahuah Elohayka (the LORD thy God); for thou hast fallen by thine iniquity* (14:1). And the Torah forbade the Egypt-and-horses reflex from the start: *he shall not multiply horses to himself, nor cause the people to return to Egypt... Ye shall henceforth return no more that way* (Deuteronomy 17:16) — so the woe is a Torah-breach. The rest Isaiah names is the rest the Formed Son holds out: *Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest. Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls* (Matthew 11:28-29). Returning to him IS the returning-and-rest the rebellious children would not take.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 26725
  FROM _s303_isa30_lookup sv, _s303_isa30_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=30 AND sv.verse_number=1
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=30 AND ev.verse_number=16
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 2 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-30-this-is-the-way-walk-ye-in-it',
       E'This is the way, walk ye in it — the Teacher''s voice restored',
       E'To a chastened people, fed *the bread of adversity, and the water of affliction* (Isaiah 30:20), the Teacher is given back: *yet shall not thy teachers be removed into a corner any more, but thine eyes shall see thy teachers* (30:20). And his voice goes before them, turn by turn: *And thine ears shall hear a word behind thee, saying, This is the way, walk ye in it, when ye turn to the right hand, and when ye turn to the left* (30:21). This is the very teaching-voice of the Psalm: *I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye* (Psalm 32:8). The Psalm names the alternative too: *Be ye not as the horse, or as the mule, which have no understanding: whose mouth must be held in with bit and bridle* (Psalm 32:9) — the same horse the rebels fled upon (Isaiah 30:16), the beast that must be reined because it will not hear. The children who *will not hear the law of Yahuah (LORD)* (30:9), who told the seers *See not* (30:10), are turned back into a people whose eyes see their teachers and whose ears hear the way. The restored Torah-instruction is the mercy on the far side of the chastening.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 26728
  FROM _s303_isa30_lookup sv, _s303_isa30_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=30 AND sv.verse_number=20
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=30 AND ev.verse_number=21
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 3 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-30-cast-them-away-as-a-menstruous-cloth',
       E'Cast them away as a menstruous cloth — the idols of silver and gold thrown off',
       E'The mark of true return is the idols cast off in disgust: *Ye shall defile also the covering of thy graven images of silver, and the ornament of thy molten images of gold: thou shalt cast them away as a menstruous cloth; thou shalt say unto it, Get thee hence* (Isaiah 30:22). Isaiah''s next chapter promises the same day: *For in that day every man shall cast away his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which your own hands have made unto you for a sin* (31:7). Hosea gives the northern house its repentant word: *Ephraim shall say, What have I to do any more with idols? I have heard him, and observed him* (14:8). And the day of Yahuah strips the handmade gods from all his people: *In that day a man shall cast his idols of silver, and his idols of gold, which they made each one for himself to worship, to the moles and to the bats* (Isaiah 2:20). The same idols of silver and gold, the work of their own hands — flung away when the Holy One of Yashar''el is feared. Return, and the idols go: *Get thee hence.*',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 26731
  FROM _s303_isa30_lookup sv, _s303_isa30_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=30 AND sv.verse_number=22
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=30 AND ev.verse_number=22
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 4 (★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_threads (slug, title, summary_md, anchor_verse_id_start, anchor_verse_id_end, tier_required, sort_order)
SELECT 'isaiah-30-the-name-of-yahuah-cometh-from-far-tophet-ordained',
       E'The name of Yahuah cometh from far — Tophet is ordained',
       E'The day has a judgment side. *Behold, the name of Yahuah (LORD) cometh from far, burning with his anger, and the burden thereof is heavy: his lips are full of indignation, and his tongue as a devouring fire* (Isaiah 30:27). And the fire is prepared: *For Tophet is ordained of old; yea, for the king it is prepared; he hath made it deep and large: the pile thereof is fire and much wood; the breath of Yahuah (LORD), like a stream of brimstone, doth kindle it* (30:33). Jeremiah names that same Tophet — the valley of the son of Hinnom, where the abominations were burned: *they have built the high places of Tophet, which is in the valley of the son of Hinnom, to burn their sons and their daughters in the fire; which I commanded them not, neither came it into my heart* (7:31). And it is turned: *it shall no more be called Tophet, nor the valley of the son of Hinnom, but the valley of slaughter* (7:32). The place of rebellion becomes the place of judgment-fire — kindled against the king and the oppressor (the Assyrian *beaten down*, 30:31). For the returning people, by contrast, the night of judgment is a feast and a song: *Ye shall have a song, as in the night when a holy solemnity is kept* (30:29), and Yahuah *bindeth up the breach of his people, and healeth the stroke of their wound* (30:26). This is covenant-lawsuit, not ethnic wrath: the fire is ordained against the system of rebellion, and the chastened remnant sings.',
       sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, 'free', 26734
  FROM _s303_isa30_lookup sv, _s303_isa30_lookup ev
 WHERE sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=30 AND sv.verse_number=27
   AND ev.edition_slug='canon' AND ev.book_slug='isaiah' AND ev.chapter_number=30 AND ev.verse_number=33
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

-- THREAD 1 members (★★)
INSERT INTO cross_reference_thread_members (thread_id, cross_reference_id, sort_order, member_note)
SELECT t.id, cr.id, 1, E'★★ *Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest* (Matthew 11:28) — the salvation of *In returning and rest shall ye be saved* (Isaiah 30:15) is the rest the Formed Son gives; returning to him IS the returning-and-rest.'
  FROM cross_reference_threads t
  JOIN _s303_isa30_lookup sv ON sv.edition_slug='canon' AND sv.book_slug='isaiah' AND sv.chapter_number=30 AND sv.verse_number=15
  JOIN _s303_isa30_lookup tv ON tv.edition_slug='canon' AND tv.book_slug='matthew' AND tv.chapter_number=11 AND tv.verse_number=28
  JOIN cross_references cr ON cr.source_verse_id=sv.verse_id AND cr.target_verse_id=tv.verse_id AND cr.source='manual'
 WHERE t.slug='isaiah-30-in-returning-and-rest-shall-ye-be-saved'
ON CONFLICT (thread_id, cross_reference_id) DO NOTHING;

